  "body": "There's a lot to love about living in Millwater, especially when everything you need is so close to home. Whether you're ready to downsize, purchasing your first home or simply looking for a more manageable lifestyle, this beautifully maintained two-bedroom unit makes an appealing choice.\r\n\r\nHaving had just one careful owner since new, the home has been exceptionally well looked after. Its practical single-level layout offers comfortable, easy living, with two bedrooms, a well-appointed bathroom and the added convenience of a dedicated car park.\r\n\r\nOutdoor living hasn't been forgotten either. With both front and rear courtyards, there's room to enjoy your morning coffee, potter with a few plants or simply sit back and enjoy a quieter moment, without the demands of a large property.\r\n\r\nThe location is another reason this home stands out. Set just back from Millwater's popular cafes and eateries, you're wonderfully positioned to enjoy the neighbourhood on foot. Better still, a medical centre and pharmacy are part of the nearby shopping precinct, bringing everyday healthcare and essential services conveniently close to home.\r\n\r\nWalking and cycling tracks, sports fields and local schools add to the appeal, while Silverdale's shopping centre, supermarkets and amenities are within easy reach. For a change of scenery, Orewa Beach is just a short drive away, and convenient motorway access keeps you well connected.\r\n\r\nFor retirees and downsizers, the appeal of ground-floor living, manageable outdoor spaces and nearby services is easy to appreciate. For first-home buyers, it's an opportunity to establish yourself in a sought-after community. And for investors, the location and practical layout offer plenty to consider.\r\n\r\nA home that's easy to care for, in a neighbourhood that's easy to love.\r\n\r\nContact Mallory and Tracey to arrange your viewing and discover what makes 16 Sapling Way such an attractive opportunity. \r\nOther agents: Conjunctional agreements are welcomed.",
